  "text": "Thank you all for those important updates. Let me summarize where we stand so we can work through this together. Ms. Bell, you've identified that the 12-workstation count in the draft won't accommodate your 16 enrolled students, and district practice calls for one workstation per student. Mr. Ortiz, the existing 20-amp circuit in Lab 3 won't support the robotics equipment -- we need a dedicated 240-volt circuit, and that needs to be added to the conversion request. Ms. Shah, the vendor requires a district-secure IoT network with wired drops, not the ordinary student Wi-Fi, and the network field in the request is currently blank. Mr. Greene, we have an $18,500 workforce-development grant restricted to capital infrastructure and equipment preparation, which can serve as our documented funding source, though we need to be mindful of the restriction when considering the additional costs for the power and network upgrades. So the key question for all of us is: can the $18,500 grant cover the cost of upgrading to 16 workstations, installing the dedicated 240-volt circuit, and setting up the secure IoT network with wired drops? I need to understand the cost implications before I can issue my decision. Mr. Ortiz and Ms. Shah, can you provide cost estimates for the power and network upgrades respectively? And Mr. Greene, can you confirm whether the grant restriction would cover all of these items?"
}
```

